658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley","html_url":"https://github.com/bendilley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-05-21T10:19:43Z","updated_at":"2020-05-21T10:19:43Z","body":"An option that could work for you is to add this to your `development` database definition in `config/database.yml`:\r\n```yaml\r\n  schema_search_path: public\r\n```\r\nThis does usually strip out the extensions altogether (and obviously anything else not in the `public` schema) but that might well be just what you want. It can be \"a string of comma-separated schema names\" according to [the API docs](https://api.rubyonrails.org/classes/ActiveRecord/ConnectionAdapters/PostgreSQL/SchemaStatements.html#method-i-schema_search_path-3D) if you have a more involved setup.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/632006710/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bendilley","id":1193658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTM2NTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1193658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendilley","html_url":"https://github.com/bendilley","fol